# Polaris Docker build context filter.
#
# Keeps `docker build` snappy and reproducible by pruning everything the
# multi-stage Dockerfiles do not need. The builder stage runs
# `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` and `pnpm --filter <name> build` from the
# repository root, so the build context must include source, package.json
# files, pnpm-workspace.yaml, pnpm-lock.yaml, and TypeScript configs — and
# nothing else of size or sensitivity.
#
# Conventions:
#   - Negation patterns (`!path`) are only used to re-include items beneath a
#     broader exclusion. We avoid them where a plain include is enough.
#   - Test artifacts and tests themselves are excluded; production images do
#     not need them, and tsconfig.json files reference test sources via the
#     `tests` rootDir which the builder image installs anyway.

# Node / pnpm install artifacts. The builder stage runs a fresh install.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store
**/.pnpm-store

# Build outputs. Always re-emitted by `pnpm --filter <name> build`.
dist
**/dist
build
**/build
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Test artifacts and snapshots.
coverage
**/coverage
.vitest
**/.vitest
**/__snapshots__
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.spec.ts

# VCS metadata. `POLARIS_GIT_SHA` is passed in as a build arg instead.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Local environment files. Production secrets are injected at runtime.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Editor / OS scratch.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea
.vscode

# Claude Code worktree / session state.
.claude

# Local-only ops files that have no business in a runtime image.
docker-compose*.yml
Makefile
README.md
USAGE.md
docs
catalog
sql
scripts/smoke
tests
resources/maxmind

# Per-package READMEs and changelogs are not needed in the image.
**/README.md
**/CHANGELOG.md
